# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-10, 2.1-11). L §3.6: "prorata shares one outflow among its parts tied on every term,
# weighted by their amounts, by rest largest at the kind's step"; "in proportion | prorata". s1 takes 10.00 from b1
# (100.00) and b2 (50.00): 6.67 and 3.33, so 93.33 and 46.67 are left (scratch/exp4.py).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind lots: place PLN min 0
  batched
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w prorata ties by k.batch.day
place konto: lots lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input b1_day: date
input b1_amt: money PLN
input b2_day: date
input b2_amt: money PLN
input s1_day: date
input s1_amt: money PLN
move b1: transfers
  on b1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount b1_amt
move b2: transfers
  on b2_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount b2_amt
move s1: transfers
  on s1_day
  leg cash from konto to shop amount s1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-04-30) of b1, bal(konto, 2026-04-30) of b2

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  b1_day = 2026-02-01
  b1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  b2_day = 2026-03-01
  b2_amt = 50.00 PLN
  s1_day = 2026-04-01
  s1_amt = 10.00 PLN
=== expect
q: (93.33 PLN, 46.67 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
